     9	- POV: Cael ≈32,800. **Lira cutaway ≈1,800** (day 53, the bar at dusk without Wind: fast, with nothing at the end of it, and the ankle). **Karis cutaway ≈1,400** (day 58, the cart-yard: "everybody knows", and the cost of not asking).
    10	- Formula load: progression vocabulary ≈82 per 10k (discharge, declaration, Iron Skin as a shout, the lattice point, the seal restated). ≈15 growth beats. Supporting beats for Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln, Pike, the steading's woman, the bowman.
    11	
    12	> **[Coordinator note 2026-10-11 — NO-SOURCE drafting, binding.]** Draft WITHOUT opening any source chapter under `books/`. The source-chapter references in the line below are retained for the coordinator's and reviewers' tools only; the author does not read them. Events come from this packet, `BOOK_MAP.md` (the plan sections, the protected-text section and the reserved-truths section) and `STATE_LEDGER.md`. Write `EVENT-LIST.md` first. Where a protected unit is quoted in the plan only in part, leave `[[TIER-B: <unit> — coordinator to supply protected text]]` and write around it. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: coordinator O3]
    13	
    14	**Read before drafting:** B7 source `chapter-03.md`, `chapter-04.md` (and `chapter-05.md` lines on days 60–70); `BOOK_MAP.md` §7 (first mover; deployment count), §8 (ford allowance), §9 (Reader Standard: the ford witness), §10; `STATE_LEDGER.md` (Movement 1 append).
    15	
    16	## Where we enter
    17	
    18	The second morning after the wall (day 51). Teague's crew went out at the previous dawn on the cold road and is a week away. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2] The five are thirteenth of thirteen with about ten marks, sleeping in the meadow. Nobody is hurt. Karis holds one word, *stillhound*, underlined.
    19	
    20	## What this movement is for
    21	
    22	The country's first rule, learned in the body and paid for in four of five, and the board pricing exactly what it cost. Turns and promises:
    23	
    24	- **"Ford's had a third."** Pike draws **one** line through Teague's name and writes five underneath: "That's arithmetic I can't do yet." Cael notices that a man never once made wrong by a crew has just written the line that might.
    25	- **The ford walked at noon** (sill, slime, the gravel bar thirty by eight, pools that fall away, the near and far shingle). Brom finds his stone with a lip. Lira runs the bar. Seln lies in the grass for two hours. **The lore:** "Dusk. Never noon."; "River's their colour."; "It's because you die." The second man must read as having got *his hand between the jaws and his throat*, not as self-harm (Reader Standard).
    26	- **The loft:** Seln's seven, and the cut dog that is never the one you're looking at. **Karis's hypothesis** (discharge; water masks it; "Evidence against: none, which I don't trust."). The plan: **bait with one declaration and kill with everything that isn't one.** "Never two at once, never the same person twice."
    27	- **The ford at dusk, ≈5,000, a learning fight:** the point; the river stands up on three sides; the pommel struck; every head but one. Brom declares Iron Skin, every head turns, he drops it like a coat, "He was still large," and the current takes the hound's hindquarters. Lira runs without a burst and is fast; the ankle goes all the way on the gravel; "I'm fine." **The pack learns** and stops testing silent bodies. Karis holds the knife by its blade with both hands rather than light a second point. **The seam:** they follow the first mover, not a leader, and the grey at the bar's tip is waiting. **One Wind burst, spent openly**, downstream and away from Karis: the landing lock with a dog in it. Seln rises out of the pool behind the grey. Five dead; **two gone downstream, logged as open.** Give the opponent its learning, and keep each decisive exchange in physical terms.
    28	- **Costs on the page:** Brom's forearm open to the bone, wrist to mid-arm; Lira's right ankle, bound flat; Karis's palms cut to the meat, unable to hold a pen; Cael's calf bitten through, in and out, felt only when the water went cold. "Four… Out of five." The bowman: "none of you shouted." **The seal log** (protected; the only restatement). Pike's line by carter; "First honest number…"
    29	- **Thornwater, days 54–58:** the calf in elevens; the ladder inventory each morning; Brom carrying nothing for the first time Cael can remember; Karis's barn-table library (three boxes made into shelves with no wall) — "everything I know about the wrong country"; **the cart-yard** (the man with the clouded eye who does not talk roads to paper; the carter's wife: "Everybody knows the quiet ground. Nobody goes in."; *everybody knows* underlined twice; "Not a good one. The first."). The grain moves.
    30	- **The road down:** the steading's woman's last word ("They stop inside, where the tiers are"); camp above the wash; Brom's cloth dark again at the wrist; **Lira at the fire**: Norhold, the ladder, "So what am I becoming, exactly, if nobody's measuring?" Nobody answers it. Cael does not either, because the same fact is his relief and her want.
    31	- **Lowmarch, day 60:** fourteen slips. Seln reads the board and takes the well: "I keep waiting for someone to ask for my report." **Brom at the plank's end:** "What does the board pay a man with no Path at all." / "Same as anyone… What'd he do?" He writes it on an old slip and keeps it against his skin, the second time in his life (Rooke was the first). Pike: "Held a dog with a shoulder and a river, that one." **The mail** sorted aloud. Hesk's letter (protected), and the grandmother he did not know about. The log. **The saying** at the book, the sheet rewritten by hand: twelfth. "Teague's still eleven up. He'll speak to you when you've cost him something."
    32	- **New on the page, days 61–69, the well on the south road.** Seln walks it first and says nothing. A small physical job with a real, mundane hazard (your choice: bad air, a stuck windlass, a fouled shaft; no monster). Four marks. Lira leans the stick against the inn wall on day 64 and walks off. Her first runs on an ankle that bends "less, and later"; fast still, with no one counting. Brom's wrist closes clean on day 66; he looks at it with the lock face and wraps it again. The money is honest (48 → 52 by the movement's end).
    33	
    34	## What must remain true / withheld
    35	
    36	- **Deployment since the Line: one** (the ford burst), from day 53 onward. No other fragment use, private or public. **Shadow unused.**
    37	- Quiet ground stays three sentences from a carter's wife. Nobody asks Pike or anyone else. No healer or Tide practitioner appears; "the nearest walks a route and she's not due" is the only reference.
    38	- The ankle never gets a healer in this movement, and it is never mended in this book.
    39	- Teague is absent: on the cold road, then back and out again on hold slips. No meeting. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2]
    40	- Karis's hypothesis becomes a *finding* only after the fight. It is entered in the log in his hand at her dictation.
    41	
    42	## What the author owns
    43	
    44	The fight's micro-geometry within the planted terrain; how the seam is seen; the barn table's details; which carter says what; the well's hazard; Lira's runs; the humor (Lira on the cart's tail announcing it was her decision; Brom's two-word sentences; Karis made to dictate). Where the Lira and Karis windows sit.
    45	
    46	## Where we leave pressure
    47	
    48	Day 69: twelfth, Teague eleven up. Four of five healing slow or wrong, with a calf, a forearm, two palms and an ankle that will never be straight. Fifty-two in hand. A rumor with two lines under it in the middle box. A board with a well's line on it and, soon, a hold's slip from a ford nobody has heard of.

