    97	- **The sale (#23; flag):** the gelding to the ferryman, for his capstan, with dry room for the three boxes in the loft over the drum as part of the price; the old capstan mule put out to grass. The cart to the smith, who means to cut its axle to mule gauge and hire it out. Brom's bill-hook came under the cart's seat board. Lira's long knife is the last thing the Book 6 purse buys. No figure is given for the sale, the purse or the reserve.
