   116	4. **Thornwater ford is not placed.** The prose says only that they forded the valley's water twice on day 43, in the light, "at shallow places with no name", and that the ford on the slip is on the road they walked. Movement 2 is free to put it where its plan needs it.
   117	5. **The carter's round trip.** Out of Thornwater at noon on day 44, riding an empty cart; back an hour past noon on day 46 ("an empty cart behind a rested mule could do in one day what a loaded one did in two"). That is how "back on the fourth" and a log dated the forty-sixth both hold. Say if the two-day road needs stricter arithmetic.
