   126	## State at movement end (for the ledger)
   127	
   128	**Calendar.** The evening of the **forty-ninth day past the Line**, in the lower inn at Lowmarch. No season, month or English weekday name is on the page; "Fifth-day" appears twice (ch4, ch5) as the academy's own word. Days on the page: 2 (night), 3, 4, 5, 6, 8, 9, 10–12, 14, 15–21 (drills; the catalogue on the 18th), 22–24, 30 (Seln, the cold road), 33, 41, 42, 43, 44–46, 48, 49. Weather: warm, dusty, long light; the roads "dry right through" from about day 46; one storm over the eastern ridge on day 33. The next movement opens on day 51.
   129	
   130	**Where everyone is.** All five at one table in the lower inn, under the wall, with one jug. They sleep in the meadow. Teague and his three are on the sill of the same room and go out on the cold road at first light on day 50 for a week.
   131	
   132	**Cael.** Eighteen, said to Pike on day 9. **Nine confirmed fragments and the uncounted anomaly** (*Still open. Still real. Patience.*, written on day 18). **Deployment since the Line: none.** No injury; the forearm is "sound again" by day 5 and is not mentioned afterward. Idle states: Shadow sealed, costing from waking, drifting at dusk (two drifts, logged as rent); Anchor asking at every sill, gate, rim and rail; Blade asking *Edge?* and taking names; Storm heavy; Wind leaning his feet. He has not read the Iron read once. The log has an entry for most days, each ending on the deployment line.
   133	
   134	**Lira.** Wind; Iron, Rank One, the certificate in her coat. Uninjured (palms skinned at the wash on day 33, healed by day 41). One burst went off by itself on the gravel bar in the first week of drills; none since. She can stop dead from a full run. She wears a long knife bought at Lowmarch's smith. She has been noticed, once, by Thornwater's bowman.
   135	
   136	**Brom.** Iron Skin; Copper "for good", said to Pike. Uninjured. Iron Skin came on the bar in drills and started and was put down at the ferry, the wash and the stretch; it did not come at all on the ladder. He carries the hedging bill. He holds the board purse's coin only when it is paid into his hand; Karis keeps it.
   137	
   138	**Karis.** Ember; Iron, Rank Three. Uninjured. Sets no points on a road. Holds: the field archive; a leaf headed *stillhound*, underlined once, with five counts and *110*; the entry of her own not-asking (day 22); the five column heads with *Outcome* underlined twice; Pike's copied line; **the carter's map**. She has asked nobody what the animal is waiting for.
   139	
   140	**Seln.** Shadow; Bronze, said once at a fire. Uninjured. Has not lifted his Path since the crossroads fire. Has walked the first part of every road out of Lowmarch (five) and out of Thornwater (three) and said so once, on day 49, in one sentence. Has the prints and the forty-five-yard line by the white stone in his head and has told nobody. **The case is on its strap, on him, shut.**
   141	
   142	**Objects and money.** Three numbered boxes, in the meadow with them on day 49 (they live in the loft over the ferryman's drum when the crew is near; they rode the Thornwater carter's cart both ways). **The cart and the gelding are sold** (day 12). **The reserve** is sealed at the bottom of the third box and has not been opened. Board purse: **eighteen marks earned** (ferry 2, fence 4, wash 3, Thornwater road 9); **about ten in hand** after one jug. Twenty pounds of flour from the steading, mostly eaten. The two letters to Hesk and Vell went west on day 4, a copper each to the turf fire. Hesk's satchel holds the log, the old volume, the observation notebook, and Pike's line on a scrap of bark. The ash wedge is still with them. The registry's printed sheet is in the middle box and was not unrolled.
   143	
   144	**Pike's book and the wall.** A heading of five names; **four lines**: *Ferry, the landing's goods. Six crossings stood. Nothing lost. Two marks.* (day 14); the fence (forty posts cut and set; four marks and flour; the saying is not on the page); the wash (three marks; not on the page); and the protected Thornwater line (day 49). **Thirteenth of thirteen; eleven lines between theirs and the top.** The top line is *Teague.* On the plank: *Thornwater ford. Clearance. Forty marks.* with *HOLD. Teague.* in Pike's capitals.
   145	
   146	**Who knows what.** The mechanism: the five, and nobody else. Pike has not asked what Cael is, and has said that he never asked. Three people have called him paper and been told yes. The party knows the word *stillhound* and nothing of what it hunts by; it has Cael's five counts, Seln's unshared reading of the ground, and the country's rule without its reason. **Nobody has heard the words "quiet ground".** Teague has read the five and found Seln on his second pass; he cannot tell what Cael is. Cael has read Teague. They have not spoken.
   147	
   148	**Open threads.** What a road hears. What the grey thing waits for. Why a hundred and ten. Why it will not cross wet gravel. The forty-mark slip, held a week for a crew that leaves at dawn, on a stretch that took two carts last month. Lira with no ladder. Brom's first earned coin. Karis's price for not asking. Seln's eight roads, waiting to bear on a day. The second question nobody put to the steading's woman. Vell, of whom Pike has never heard. The hook and the bar.

