   132	
   133	Lira looked along the plank again, more slowly. He watched her understand it, and it was not a happy understanding. She had gone up a ladder a rung at a time since she was a girl, at Fenmark and in a yard and on a hill, and had paid for every rung with her feet.
   134	
   135	"Then where do you go up?" she said.
   136	
   137	"I don't think you do."
   138	
   139	"Somebody's best. Somebody's always best. How does anyone know who?"
   140	
   141	"You ask who came back," said a voice behind them.
