   147	The left sleeve of his coat was folded and pinned at the elbow, neatly, with a brass pin gone dull. Under the right arm he carried a tall book in boards, and he had a pen behind his ear. He was broad and not tall, with a grey stubble and a brown bald head, and his eyes were the colour of the tar on the plank.
