   170	
   171	"We want work," said Lira. "There's no bouts. What do crews do, here?"
   172	
   173	"Walk, carry, climb, fight."
   174	
   175	"In that order?"
   176	
   177	"Depends on the day."
   178	
   179	He dipped the pen, and he had a way of doing it without looking, down into the hole and up, that must have taken him a year to learn.
   180	
   181	"Who's captain?"
