    24	
    25	It was strange to hear. Cael had read those words on a scrap of bark in a hold's yard, and thought them his; and now they belonged to a woman with a board of loaves on her head, and a man mending a trace, and an old carter under a tree, who had lifted his chin at the word *stretch* and held it there to the end. Several of the people at the plank turned and looked at the five of them. They looked once, at their boots and their steel, and then went back to their own affairs.
    26	
