    62	
    63	She had gone and read it.
    64	
    65	It was her page. Her name stood at its head in his square capitals, and under it the figures, the trial and the hall's seal and the oak, each with its date. Below the figures were the two words he had written and never shown her; she had spent a term guessing at them, and had guessed kinder words than these.
    66	
    67	The first was *Late.* He had drawn one line through it. Under it, on the day after the Blade, he had written the other, which was *Hers.*
