   232	
   233	That was the whole of it. Cael read it three times and copied it into the log verbatim and sat for a while with the pen not moving, in a loft that smelled of grain, under a roof that no chancellor had endowed and no charter governed, and then he wrote the entry.
   234	
   235	*Forty-sixth day. Thornwater. First roof since the Line.*
