   238	
   239	*The stretch. Five items, written above, and the ruling on every one is the same: it did what it did because we did nothing. A carter's word for it, one word, entered as a word and not as a fact, because a name is the least I know about anything.*
   240	
   241	*Claim: there is something out here that hunts Paths. Evidence: one mile, one buckle, a hundred paces of gravel it would not cross, and a man who has walked that road for twenty years and hires crews for what they don't do. Ruling: hold — and write the claim down anyway, because I have been not-using mine in front of hostile audiences since I was fifteen, and four institutions marked me down for it, and a valley just priced it as the only competence on the road. Turns out that was training for this.*
   242	
   243	*Lira could have cleared it and said so once. Brom held a mule. Karis looked and did not light. Seln said five sentences in a mile and none of them was a reason. Five people held everything they own for a mile of road in the dark, and nobody had to be told twice, and that is the finding of the six weeks: we are a unit in a country that has never seen one.*
   244	
   245	*Hesk's satchel is on my knee. It has been through a ford and two carts and a wash and it sits flat, which is what he made it to do. He said mind the shape. The shape out here is a road, and a board, and one line in a book, and I can see all of it.*
   246	
   247	*Note the date. Season's open, and for once it isn't theirs.*

