editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-06.md:47:"Delivered at my fence," she said. "And nothing lost that I can see. I'll stand to that." She gave the slip back to the cart. "There's a loft over the barn. The grain goes up in the morning, and you can have what room it leaves. Ladder's sound."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-06.md:49:"We're obliged," said Brom.
