   278	
   279	The woman with the dough had gone back to her pan. She had heard it, though, and so had the man with the harness across his knees, and the three children; and by dark, Cael supposed, the whole meadow would know that five strangers had stood on a boat all day and lost nothing. It was not much to be known for. It was also the first thing that anybody east of a line knew about them at all, and it happened to be true.
   280	
   281	It bought flour, and salt, and a piece of bacon no bigger than a hand, and Brom told them that it would have kept the gelding for one day and the half of another. Karis wrote the line into the field archive as she had heard it said, and drew her second rule under two of its words.
   282	
