   111	She had come up the bank with her hair stuck to her forehead, and she was reading over his arm as she had read over it since Ardenmere. Brom had the same leave. Karis, who sat ten feet away with her stone, saw what he showed her and never once looked at the book.
   112	
   113	"Six. Compression doesn't charge, and Blade only asks."
   114	
   115	"It's a good deal of rent, for a man with no income."
   116	
   117	"I've two marks."
   118	
   119	"You've two-fifths of two marks, and you ate it." She dropped down beside him and pulled off a boot. "Does it ever stop? The saying no?"
   120	
