276:- Ch6: *Eightieth day. Lira's leg is straight. The boxes are ours. The cart is in the gorge. A healer came up the road because a carter said we were late.*
277:- Ch7: *Teague priced us. He's right about the cart. Oryn read me three times and got nothing three times and wants a fourth. Two people out here measuring me, and neither of them has a seal. I keep waiting to mind.*
278:- Ch8, Part-1 summary (EXC-B7-001): *Twelve weeks. Seven contracts. Pike says there's ground out here where the Arbiter goes quiet, and nobody goes in twice. Karis has been waiting her whole life for a sentence like that. Seln says the contract was written by someone from inside. I say it pays. Two days east, through Thornwater, on the day the healer said. For twelve weeks nothing out here has read me. I'd like to see what a place that reads nothing does with that.*
284:- Ch14, the birthday line: *Hundred and second day past the Line. Nineteen. Written at Thornwater, in the steading's common room, the fire lit for us. Witnesses: four of my own, and a healer who's a stop.* [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]
293:- Ch22, the stake paid: *Teague sat down next to me. Asked what I am. I could have read him. I asked instead. The day I stop asking is the day I'm the registry. Write it down. Again. Every time.*
301:- Ch4: the carter's wife: "You mean the quiet ground? Everybody knows the quiet ground. Nobody goes in." — Lira: "So what am I becoming, exactly, if nobody's measuring?" — Seln: "I keep waiting for someone to ask for my report." — Brom: "What does the board pay a man with no Path at all." / Pike: "Same as anyone," … "What'd he do?" — Pike: "Teague's still eleven up. He'll speak to you when you've cost him something. That's not rudeness. That's the ledger."
304:- Ch7: Oryn: "That's a tape and a season. It'll set." — "Twenty days," … "Round. Two at a hold, near enough, and the road between, and the road's the part that doesn't move." — "I remember who I've had my hands on," … "That's the book. A healer who needs a page to know who's owed has stopped looking at them." — "In the city I healed Bronzes with bruises. Out here I set legs. I'm not going back and I'm not stopping. The route is the only thing I own." — "It's like putting my hands in a river in the dark. Something's moving. I can't find the banks, so I can't read it, so I can't touch it. That's the rule. I didn't make it." — "When you're not broken, I run the long one. It won't read you either. I want to feel it not read you properly." — "Thornwater's on my route in nine days. You'll be on the board by then. Come find me. I want to read you when you're not broken." / "Nine days." — The ford-keeper: "Then they go round," … "That's worth seventy to know before the first cart's in the gorge. I'd sooner pay it for this." — Teague: "You cleared Thornwater's ford with five and lost a cart on the high bench with five." / "Yes." / "The ford was good work. The bench was a cart." … "The board's going to have you and me on the same contract inside a season. Be good enough that I'm glad."
307:- Ch10: Karis: "Sixty-two cords and twenty strides," … "One thousand three hundred and seventy-four yards, and a piece." … "A circle is a made shape." — Lira: "like a clock that stopped and started again without losing the time." — Seln: "You drive them where you've measured to. Not where you've measured from." … "Five years in the weather. A cold term either side." — Brom: "Skin." — Karis: "It costs nothing. There's nothing to spend." — Seln: "I've a knife and fifteen years. It was never most of what I do." — Oryn: "Nothing. Not nothing in him. Nothing in my hands." … "A healer's hands stop working there." — Cael: "It was dark before," … "It's dark now." — Karis: "None I own. And I own more than the registry prints." — Seln: "They live in here because nothing that walks in can fight." [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]
311:- Ch14: "So I couldn't read you because there was nothing in you shaped like a Path for the reading to find." / "I don't know. Maybe." / "I don't know either. I'm a healer, not a theorist." … "What I know is you've now got a piece of the thing I read with." / "Yes." … "Then use it on yourself first. Before anyone." … "I want to know what you find, and I want to be the one you tell." — Oryn: "And when it turns outward, you ask. Every time. I ask the dying." / "I ask first. Every time." — Karis: "You have an instrument now. It's not mine. It never will be. I'm entering that I know that." — Oryn: "A stop," … "Good. Write it down before it changes." — Seln: "Six went in. Six came out. He's counted her." … "So has the broker."
314:- Ch17: Pike: "Eleventh. Teague's ten up." … "I'd not take it." — Seln: "That's not a wage. That's a lure, cut to fit." … "This isn't a contract. It's a pre-restriction inventory. They've mapped what we do inside, and they've priced a floor where we can't do it." / Karis: "They don't know about Cael." / "They don't need to." … "They want the case. The boy's the price of the case." — "They'll send people. A lure's no use if nobody's waiting at the end of it. People have faces. Six years I've wanted a face." — Cael: "Inside the circle, I'm the only one who works. They chose a floor that makes the rest of you helpless. They don't know it doesn't do anything to me." — Brom: "Doors open both ways," … "I don't like it. I'm in." — Lira: "I want it entered that I said walk away. I was right. We're going anyway." — Teague: "You're taking the Stair contract." / "Yes," Cael said. / "It's a bad contract." / "Yes." … "My crew's at Millrace in two days," Teague said. "If you're late back, we'll come look." / "Noted." [OWNER-pending #50]
315:- Ch18: Oryn: "No." … "You asked. That's the rule and you kept it. The answer's no. Next." — "You're asking me to break the route," / "I'm not asking. I'm telling you where we'll be." / "That's worse. That's a healer's sentence." — "I'm not going to be anybody's sixth." — **Terms:** "You're on the route now. Which means when I say lie still, you lie still, and when I say I can't help you, you believe me." — "Well?" / "May I read you?" / "Yes. That's the answer, and I'm the one giving it…" — "You're built to arrive." / "Yes," she said. "That's what I am." — Lira: "He asked twice and got one," / Brom: "That's the rate," — Seln: "Newer. This one's been re-surveyed."
316:- Ch19: Brom: "Ridge," — Seln: "They can shoot the bowl," … "They can't shoot the stair." — Oryn: "I can see what's wrong. I can't feel it and I can't touch it. Tape it. Leave the bolt." … "the bolt's the plug" … "I came south for exactly this. Enter that." — Oryn: "Ask first," — Lira: "Later." / "Later." — Oryn at the stone: "There. Back," … "The clock started again." — "It held a stair. It's not going to hold anything else this season." — Seln: "No faces." — Teague: "You walked out of the Quiet declaring," / "Yes." … "Then you're not on the board anymore. You're something the board doesn't have a column for."
