   361	He was a man of forty or so, of the middle height, heavy in the forearm, with hair cropped close and gone grey over the ears. He had stopped on the sill before he came in. That was the first item, and Cael put the most weight on it. Three people had stopped behind him in the same instant, at the same distances, without a word; and for the length of a breath the man's eyes had gone nowhere at all, while he listened to them be there. He had counted his own before he counted the room.
