+| The ship-oak plank and its materials | **KEEP** | Consistent with Pike's public, low-paper institution and later board scenes (`manuscript/chapter-02.md:85-113,161-163`). |
+| How a ledger line is made and paid | **KEEP** | The before/after reading, witness correction and iron-box payment support rather than contradict later packet mechanics (`manuscript/chapter-03.md:251-277`; `manuscript/chapter-07.md:29-91`). |
+| Sailcloth wall, thirteen lines, mule-named crew | **KEEP** | Matches the fixed day-49 board track and leaves later rewrites available (`manuscript/chapter-07.md:181-191`). |
