   123	- **Carried tools and papers:** Brom has the hedging bill and ash wedge; Lira has the long knife; Karis has the dry carter's map and the still-rolled registry sheet; Hesk's satchel has the logs, notebook and Pike's bark line, while the Hesk/Vell letters have gone west (`manuscript/chapter-03.md:123-129`; `manuscript/chapter-04.md:311-331`; `manuscript/chapter-06.md:165-169,195-223`; `manuscript/chapter-01.md:159-197`).
   124	- **Local relationship continuity:** the hide-woman is the same person who gave the cake and hired the wash recovery; Thornwater's woman, bowman and carter have already seen the crew hold; the carter gave Karis his twenty-two-year map in exchange for Brom's wheel repair (`manuscript/chapter-02.md:3-5`; `manuscript/chapter-04.md:285-353`; `manuscript/chapter-06.md:13-55,187-211`).
