+
+**Flag 6, “the rule is a road rule” — KEEP.** Lowmarch openly permits fires, voices and native Paths in its meadow, while the steading distinguishes a yard fire from a point at its fence (`manuscript/chapter-02.md:55-63`; `manuscript/chapter-04.md:165-183`). This is a cultural road precaution, not the later scientific finding that stillhounds hunt Path discharge. Later planned declarations in fights and at surveyed sites remain compatible.
+
+**Flag 8, buckle and signal — AMEND only the hearing conclusion.** The buckle test itself is a valid observation: the head casts when the buckle stops and settles when it resumes (`manuscript/chapter-05.md:229-233`). “It hears. As a dog does” improperly converts that observation into a known auditory sense and conflicts with the ledger's day-53 mechanism release (`manuscript/chapter-05.md:235`). Seln's “waiting upon a signal” remains a clearly marked professional analogy whose final sentence is that he does not know the signal, so it may stand (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:133-139`). Likewise “waiting to be told something” remains metaphor rather than mechanism (`manuscript/chapter-07.md:291`). Fix 1 removes only the premature sense finding.
+
+**Flag 9, board “nearly full” — KEEP.** It describes physical oak coverage on day 49, not a fixed slip count, and a high-turnover board can validly carry fourteen slips on day 60 (`manuscript/chapter-07.md:103-111`). No later count is forced.
+
+## 7. Names
+
+**PASS.** No unplanned person, place or animal receives a proper name in `manuscript/chapter-01.md:1-367` through `manuscript/chapter-07.md:1-383`. Pike, Teague, Lowmarch, Thornwater and inherited western names are already supplied canon. “Red not-pine,” “north water,” “cold road,” “turf fire,” the unnamed gelding and the crew labels are descriptions, not owner-consuming proper names (`manuscript/chapter-01.md:75-87`; `manuscript/chapter-03.md:39-49`; `manuscript/chapter-07.md:299-307`). The Thornwater carter, courier, ferryman, smith, broker, captains, steading people, bowman and Teague's spear/bow/boy all remain unnamed (`manuscript/chapter-01.md:141-193`; `manuscript/chapter-03.md:63-129,195-205`; `manuscript/chapter-06.md:3-55`; `manuscript/chapter-07.md:29-91,299-307`).
+
+## 8. Movement 2 inheritance not already carried by its packet
+
+Movement 2 must inherit these surviving-prose facts in addition to its own explicit entry paragraph:
+
+- **Road culture is contextual:** ordinary meadow/yard use is open, while travel roads and exposed fence-lines trigger the hold. Do not retroactively make Lowmarch's meadow silent or Pathless (`manuscript/chapter-02.md:55-63`; `manuscript/chapter-04.md:165-183`).
+- **The companions have failed before succeeding at the hold:** Lira has one involuntary practice burst, Brom has let Iron Skin rise and put it down, and Karis has lit at ninety and later held unlit to three hundred. These are native-Path events, not additions to Cael's deployment count (`manuscript/chapter-04.md:21-65`; `manuscript/chapter-05.md:7`).
+- **The stillhound file is divided:** Karis has the name, five observations and 110; Seln privately has palm-wide prints, the forty-five-yard follower spacing and an explicitly unknown signal; neither has the discharge mechanism (`manuscript/chapter-05.md:221-257`; `manuscript/chapter-06.md:107-139,217-223`).
+- **Lowmarch's working geography and institutions persist:** cable ferry/capstan, lower inn/eave/plank, upper inn, smith, meadow/ash, road fan, public read-before/read-after procedure, iron payment box, sailcloth wall and Pike's double look (`manuscript/chapter-02.md:13-87,145-163`; `manuscript/chapter-03.md:251-277`; `manuscript/chapter-07.md:29-63,181-219`).
+- **Asset state after #23:** no cart or horse; the reserve is sealed under masonry chips in the third box and opens only by all five; the boxes lodge over the ferry drum when the crew is near Lowmarch; Seln's closed case is back on its strap (`manuscript/chapter-03.md:107,123-185`; `manuscript/chapter-04.md:277`; `manuscript/chapter-05.md:55-65`).
+- **Carried tools and papers:** Brom has the hedging bill and ash wedge; Lira has the long knife; Karis has the dry carter's map and the still-rolled registry sheet; Hesk's satchel has the logs, notebook and Pike's bark line, while the Hesk/Vell letters have gone west (`manuscript/chapter-03.md:123-129`; `manuscript/chapter-04.md:311-331`; `manuscript/chapter-06.md:165-169,195-223`; `manuscript/chapter-01.md:159-197`).
